text:
In deep ocean blue,
Gentle giant whale swims by;
Nature's harmony.

Noble walnut tree,
Roots deeply in Earth's embrace;
Time's silent witness.

Whale beneath the sea,
Sings a haunting, melodic tune;
Echoes through waters.

Walnut tree stands tall,
Leaves whisper secrets to the breeze;
Ancient, wise sentinel.

Whale breaches the waves,
In awe-inspiring dance meets sky;
Freedom's grand display.

Tree's branches sway gently,
Offering shelter and shade;
Life's cradle and home.

Together they live,
In different realms, yet united;
Nature's poetic verse.

Through seasons they thrive,
Witness to each other's strength;
Life's enduring story.

Haiku captures brief;
A moment where worlds converge,
Whale and walnut tree.
